      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2016 AWHONN, the Association of Women\u2019s Health, Obstetric and Neonatal Nurses.",
        "AbstractText": "Hair-thread tourniquets are a rare occurrence but result in significant injury as a hair or thread wraps around a digit, resulting in tissue swelling, pain, or possible tissue ischemia. This condition is often overlooked in the differential diagnosis for a fussy infant. Awareness of this condition will help nurses and other clinicians identify and treat the condition. Some simple prevention strategies can help parents and other caregivers mitigate risk."
      },
